{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","generated":true,"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo","roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" captures state snapshots before each undoable action. Undo history lives in memory (lost on relaunch), but restored state is persisted normally via "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restore(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you don’t use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":", nothing changes. It’s fully opt-in.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Adding Undo to Your App","type":"heading","anchor":"Adding-Undo-to-Your-App","level":2},{"text":"1. Create the plugin","type":"heading","anchor":"1-Create-the-plugin","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass declarative predicates to classify which actions are undoable and which coalesce:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let isUndoable: @Sendable (AppAction) -> Bool = { action in","    switch action {","    case .items(.create), .items(.delete), .items(.rename): true","    case .selectItem, .toggleSidebar: false","    }","}","","let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    isUndoable: isUndoable,","    coalescing: { action in","        if case .items(.rename) = action { return true }","        return false","    }",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"text":"2. Register and pass to Store","type":"heading","anchor":"2-Register-and-pass-to-Store","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Register the plugin with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for lifecycle hooks, and pass it directly to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for undo\/redo methods and ","type":"text"},{"code":"canUndo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"canRedo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracking:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)","","return Store(","    initialState: AppState(),","    reducer: { state, action in","        reducer.reduce(state: &state, action: action, environment: environment)","    },","    plugins: plugins,","    undoPlugin: undoPlugin,","    persistencePlugin: persistencePlugin,","    isUndoable: isUndoable",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" handles the rest internally: snapshotting state before undoable actions, restoring via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"applyRestore"},{"type":"text","text":" on undo\/redo, draining persistence changes, and updating "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canUndo"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canRedo"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"3. Wire platform UI","level":3,"anchor":"3-Wire-platform-UI"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"macOS"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — replace the Edit menu:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["WindowGroup { ... }",".commands {","    CommandGroup(replacing: .undoRedo) {","        Button(\"Undo\") { store.undo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: .command)","            .disabled(!store.canUndo)","        Button(\"Redo\") { store.redo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: [.command, .shift])","            .disabled(!store.canRedo)","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"iOS","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — bridge the system UndoManager for shake-to-undo:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ In your view — connect the environment UndoManager:",".onAppear { store.undoManager = undoManager }",".onChange(of: undoManager) { _, new in store.undoManager = new }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" automatically registers undo\/redo actions with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndoManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" after each undoable dispatch.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Coalescing","level":2,"anchor":"Coalescing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"coalescing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" predicate groups consecutive matching actions into a single undo step. The first coalescing action captures a snapshot; subsequent consecutive coalescing actions share that snapshot. A non-coalescing action or undo\/redo resets the flag. Typing “hello” produces one undo entry, not five.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Undo and sync","level":2,"anchor":"Undo-and-sync"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Undo is scoped to changes the local user made. If another device deletes an entity and the merge surfaces that mid-session, ","type":"text"},{"code":"restore(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" will not bring the row back, even though older undo snapshots still contain it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That has to be the rule, because the alternative is worse than a missing undo step: restoring the row records it as a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"creation"}]},{"type":"text","text":", which syncs out and re-seeds every peer that had already agreed it was gone. One person’s undo would undo everybody’s delete."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" tracks this in "},{"code":"remotelyRemovedIDs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". An ID leaves the set the moment it becomes local again — the user creates it, or the row reappears on disk because the other device undid "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"its","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" delete — so nothing is permanently un-undoable. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the mechanics."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apps that don’t sync never hit this: nothing populates the set, and undo behaves exactly as it always has."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Memory","text":"Memory","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each snapshot is a value-type copy of your state. Cost is proportional to the number of entities across all stores. Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxDepth","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to bound memory for large state:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(maxDepth: 50, ...)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Public API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"title":"EntityStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"PluginHost","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","abstract":[{"text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"title":"Persistence Middleware"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Troubleshooting":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Troubleshooting","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"title":"Swidux","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Macros","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","abstract":[{"text":"Reference for ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration."}],"role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"title":"EntityStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginAnalyticsReference":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","title":"UndoPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"type":"topic","title":"Getting Started with Swidux","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","abstract":[{"text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observation layer."}],"title":"Store"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","abstract":[{"text":"API surface for the ","type":"text"},{